[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m To solve the problem, we need to find the sum of all integer bases \( b > 9 \) such that \( 17_b \) is a divisor of \( 97_b \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m First, we convert the numbers from base \( b \) to decimal:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m - \( 17_b = 1 \cdot b + 7 = b + 7 \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m - \( 97_b = 9 \cdot b + 7 = 9b + 7 \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m We need \( b + 7 \) to divide \( 9b + 7 \). This translates to the condition:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m \[ (b + 7) \mid (9b + 7) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m Using the division algorithm, we express this as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m \[ \frac{9b + 7}{b + 7} = k \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m where \( k \) is an integer. Simplifying this, we find:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m \[ 9b + 7 = k(b + 7) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m \[ 9b + 7 = kb + 7k \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m \[ (9 - k)b + (7 - 7k) = 0 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m \[ (9 - k)b = 7(k - 1) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m \[ b = \frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m We also find that:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m \[ b = \frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m which simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m \[ b = 7 + \frac{56}{b + 7} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m This implies \( b + 7 \) must be a divisor of 56. The divisors of 56 greater than 16 (since \( b > 9 \)) are 28 and 56. Therefore:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m - If \( b + 7 = 28 \), then \( b = 21 \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m - If \( b + 7 = 56 \), then \( b = 49 \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m Thus, the valid bases are 21 and 49. Summing these, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78217)[0m \[ 21 + 49 = 70 \]
